<%#
  Mounts the Paddle overlay for a pending record. Shared by the booking and the
  order flows: everything specific to what is being bought is already resolved
  into `checkout` by the controller, so this only has to hand it over.

  Empty when checkout couldn't be prepared, so the turbo stream still clears any
  previous one.

  The toast copy is resolved here rather than in the controller: Stimulus has no
  `t()`, and these strings are shown to buyers on both the Polish and the English
  site.

  The Paddle credentials ride along for the same reason. Paddle.js is no longer
  in the layout — it is fetched only when a checkout opens, so what used to be
  the layout's `Paddle.Initialize` arguments have to reach the controller from
  here. `client_token` is a public, client-side token; the API key is not and
  never leaves the server.

  locals: checkout
%>
<%= tag.div id: "paddle_checkout", data: (checkout && {
      controller: "paddle",
      paddle_token_value: Pay::PaddleBilling.client_token,
      paddle_environment_value: Pay::PaddleBilling.environment,
      paddle_items_value: checkout[:items].to_json,
      paddle_custom_data_value: checkout[:custom_data].to_json,
      paddle_customer_id_value: checkout[:customer_id],
      paddle_success_url_value: checkout[:success_url],
      paddle_abandon_url_value: checkout[:abandon_url],
      paddle_open_failed_title_value: t("paddle.open_failed_title"),
      paddle_blocked_message_value: t("paddle.blocked"),
      paddle_retry_message_value: t("paddle.retry"),
      paddle_error_title_value: t("paddle.error_title"),
      paddle_error_fallback_value: t("paddle.error_fallback")
    }) %>
